      "writtenOn": "2026-11-20T06:40:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "**Medium**: pruning is keyed on \"credentials currently complete\" rather than \"relation still exists\". `ceph_access_data_by_app` omits relations whose secret cannot be read (SecretNotFoundError, not yet granted, rotated) so their `ceph-access.\u003capp\u003e` entries are set to None and the libvirt secret is undefined while VMs may still have RBD volumes attached (also the AttributeError path at :1350-1353). Fix: prune only apps no longer in `self.model.relations[\"ceph-access\"]`; leave related-but-incomplete entries untouched; add a test.",
      "revId": "c0703ee01050ad476bc9baa43f64af281a857697",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7e13cce0_5bb677d1",
        "filename": "charms/openstack-hypervisor/src/charm.py",
