        "id": 37697
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-20T06:40:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "**Medium**: the charm now always writes `ceph-access.\u003capp\u003e` keys that only snap-openstack-hypervisor PR #235 understands, with no snap revision/channel guard. Against an older snap the keys are ignored or rejected by the configure hook (unit error). Fix: confirm #235 is in the default tracked channel and state it in the commit message, or skip writing these keys when unsupported.",
      "revId": "c0703ee01050ad476bc9baa43f64af281a857697",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "60f34107_4d0ffe92",
        "filename": "charms/openstack-hypervisor/src/charm.py",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 1361,
      "author": {
        "id": 35761
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-19T21:11:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A backend can drop out of backends while its relation still exists, for example when the Juju secret lookup returns SecretNotFoundError. This unsets the snap entry and can lead to deletion of a working libvirt secret. Can we keep the last applied value while credentials are unavailable and prune only when the relation is gone?\n\nhttps://review.opendev.org/c/openstack/sunbeam-charms/+/1009338/5/charms/storage/cinder-volume-ceph/lib/charms/cinder_volume_ceph/v0/ceph_access.py#204\nhttps://github.com/canonical/snap-openstack-hypervisor/blob/3390e7b000d2b84e95099a1681df171d752571c3/openstack_hypervisor/hooks.py#L2331",
      "revId": "c0703ee01050ad476bc9baa43f64af281a857697",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543"
    },
